---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="The Power of Gaming — Krishna Soni" description="The Power of Gaming: A Journey Through The World Of Gaming And How It Enhances Us by Krishna Soni (Krizekster).">
  <section class="section-wrap grid gap-12 lg:grid-cols-[.8fr_1.2fr] lg:items-center">
    <div data-parallax="-0.06" class="mx-auto w-full max-w-sm rounded-[.7rem_1.75rem_1.75rem_.7rem] bg-[#31433a] p-6 shadow-[1.2rem_1.2rem_0_#becbb9] sm:p-9">
      <div class="flex min-h-[29rem] flex-col justify-between border border-paper/35 p-6 text-paper sm:min-h-[35rem] sm:p-8">
        <p class="font-mono text-[.62rem] uppercase tracking-[.12em] text-mist">Krishna Soni (Krizekster) / Feb 2025</p>
        <h1 class="text-[clamp(3.2rem,6vw,5.5rem)] font-extrabold leading-[.78] tracking-[-.1em]">The<br />Power<br />of<br /><span class="text-[#d5e0cb]">Gaming</span></h1>
        <p class="font-mono text-[.62rem] uppercase tracking-[.1em] text-mist">Publisher: Kri Zek LLC • 481 Pages</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Book / 05</p>
      <h2 data-parallax="0.04" class="mt-4 text-[clamp(2.8rem,6vw,6rem)] font-extrabold leading-[.84] tracking-[-.09em]">The Power of Gaming: A Journey Through The World Of Gaming And How It Enhances Us</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 font-mono text-xs text-sage-deep">By Krishna Soni (Krizekster) • Published February 2025 • Kri Zek LLC</p>
      <p class="mt-5 max-w-2xl text-base leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">Backed by 100+ research studies, <em>The Power of Gaming</em> explores how game worlds, cognitive feedback loops, and interactive systems enhance human potential. Crowdfunded and launched across the USA, UK, Germany, Sweden, and Japan.</p>
      
      <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-4">
        <a href="https://play.google.com/store/books/details?id=J1GUEQAAQBAJ" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="button button-dark" data-magnetic data-magnetic-strength="0.35">
          <span class="magnetic-text">Get Ebook on Google Play Books ↗</span>
        </a>
        <a href="#chapters" class="button button-light" data-magnetic data-magnetic-strength="0.3">
          <span class="magnetic-text">Explore Chapter Themes ↓</span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="chapters" class="border-y border-line bg-[#e4e9df]">
    <div class="section-wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">Inside the book</p>
      <h2 data-parallax="0.03" class="section-heading mt-3">Interactive worlds are carefully held systems.</h2>
      <div class="mt-12 grid gap-px overflow-hidden rounded-[1.35rem] border border-line bg-line md:grid-cols-2">
        <article class="bg-paper p-7 sm:p-9"><p class="eyebrow">01 / Neuroscience</p><h3 class="mt-5 text-3xl font-bold leading-[.95] tracking-[-.07em]">Why places players remember feel coherent.</h3><p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">The rules, atmosphere, and small details that turn a collection of assets into a world with its own logic, backed by 100+ scientific studies.</p></article>
        <article class="bg-paper p-7 sm:p-9"><p class="eyebrow">02 / Telemetry &amp; Feedback</p><h3 class="mt-5 text-3xl font-bold leading-[.95] tracking-[-.07em]">Every action needs a meaningful response.</h3><p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">How high-frequency feedback loops invite attention, build cognitive trust, and create the feeling that an experience is truly alive.</p></article>
        <article class="bg-paper p-7 sm:p-9"><p class="eyebrow">03 / Story &amp; Agency</p><h3 class="mt-5 text-3xl font-bold leading-[.95] tracking-[-.07em]">Narrative is structure, not decoration.</h3><p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">A look at the frameworks that give choices, spaces, and player decisions a reason to matter together under friction.</p></article>
        <article class="bg-paper p-7 sm:p-9"><p class="eyebrow">04 / Cognitive Transfer</p><h3 class="mt-5 text-3xl font-bold leading-[.95] tracking-[-.07em]">Bringing the lessons back to real-world potential.</h3><p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">Translating play, progression, and world-building into cognitive metrics, deep work, and better software tools.</p></article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Second Book: The Balancing Factor (In Progress) -->
  <section class="section-wrap border-t border-line">
    <div class="max-w-3xl">
      <p class="eyebrow">Second Book / In Progress</p>
      <h2 data-parallax="0.03" class="section-heading mt-3">The Balancing Factor</h2>
      <p class="mt-2 font-mono text-xs text-sage-deep">By Krishna Soni • Currently Drafting</p>
      <p class="display-copy mt-6">
        Non-fiction exploration of psychological, physiological, and emotional balance. Scientifically grounded, creatively unbound.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-6 font-mono text-xs text-ink-soft">
        <span class="rounded bg-paper-deep px-3 py-1.5 font-bold">In-Progress — Drafting Phase</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
